Proof verifier

dist/verify-proof/verifier.wasm, which pearljs/verify-proof loads, is compiled from Rust: zk-pow and pearl-blake3 from Pearl's fp8-scheme branch (commit 1dd75a52e073b4a67079c7b6758228d71865ccea), under the ISC License above, with the changes in wasm/patches; Pearl's fork of plonky2 and starky, under the MIT License (Copyright (c) 2022-2025 The Plonky2 Authors, Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Pearl Research Labs) or the Apache License 2.0; and crates from crates.io under the terms each names, MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, Zlib, Unlicense, CC0-1.0, MIT-0 and Unicode-3.0 among them. dist/verify-proof/LICENSES.txt holds the licence text each of those crates ships, and wasm/licenses.py writes it from the build's dependency graph. v2-cache.bin and v4-cache.bin beside it are the verifier setups zk-pow's build_cache generates from the same source.
